	(text "MCP4728: internal 2.048 V ref x2 gain, VDD = 3.3 V so outputs saturate near 3.3 V - keep codes <= 3.2 V.\nEEPROM power-up defaults: DAC1-3 = max code (lowest VS); DAC0 (boost) = 0 V so nothing is injected into the boost FB while MAIN_IN is absent (USB-only).\nPCA9538: IO0-3 enables (10k pull-downs keep every converter off at power-up), IO4-7 read the build straps (0R to GND = block fitted, 100k pull-up otherwise)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 400 446 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "45e8402b-501e-4f6d-b7ce-57f6926b5634")
	)
	(text "HVBUS = MAIN_IN through SS310 (pass-through) and/or the boost converter. Per driver: fit the LM5164 buck block OR the 0R link (R44-R46) to HVBUS, never both.\nDEFAULT POPULATION: pass-through + 0R links. The boost block (U12) and the three per-driver buck blocks (U15-U17) are DNP, with their strap resistors,\nso the firmware reads them as not fitted."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 262 225 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "40862e5d-b35d-42a1-9fd8-7777f8ecdbd5")
	)
